(1467983371822208,1467983199560832,18,'assistant',NULL,'Interesting: there are 3 tables matching in some schema (4 chars schema name — likely \"test\" or similar), but the connected db is lemon_cms (9 chars). The tables matching \'%changelog%\' exist in a different schema. Let me check which schema. Data is masked but I can query with aggregate/COUNT to get names? The masking applies to string values. Hmm, `<str:25chars>` — table name length 25 chars. \"act_app_databasechangeloglock\" is 29 chars. And there\'s one with 14 chars — likely \"DATABASECHANGELOG\" is 17. Hmm.\n\nLet me think: 29 chars = \"act_app_databasechangeloglock\" (a,c,t,_,a,p,p,_ = 8; databasechangeloglock = 20 → 28. Let me count precisely: \"act_\" =4, \"app_\"=4 → 8, \"databasechangeloglock\" = \"database\"(8)+\"changelog\"(9)+\"lock\"(4)=21 → total 29. Yes! 29 chars matches.\n\nAnd 25 chars: \"act_app_databasechangelog\" = 8 + \"databasechangelog\"(17) = 25. Yes!\n\n14 chars: \"DATABASECHANGELOG\" is 17. Hmm, 14 chars... maybe \"act_app_lock\"? no. Could be \"databasechangelog\" = 17. What about \"ACT_APP_...\"? Let me check: 14 chars could be \"databasechange\" no.\n\nAnyway, the schema is 4 chars — not \"lemon_cms\" (9). So the table exists in another database on the same instance. Let me confirm by querying with a filter and counting per schema, and get column info. But data is masked so I can\'t read schema name directly. I could use LENGTH or compare: check if TABLE_SCHEMA = \'lemon_cms\'. Let me run a query that returns booleans/counts which aren\'t masked strings... Actually counts are numbers, likely not masked. Masking seems applied to string values.\n\nLet me query: SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA=\'lemon_cms\' AS in_lemon, TABLE_NAME ... hmm table_name is string masked. Better: use conditional aggregation to get counts.\n\nLet\'s do: SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_NAME LIKE \'%changelog%\' GROUP BY TABLE_SCHEMA — schema string masked but I can test with WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA=\'lemon_cms\'.\n\nActually, more useful: get the columns of act_app_databasechangeloglock via information_schema and check if it exists in lemon_cms.\n\nLet me run:\nSELECT COUNT(*) c FROM information_schema.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA=\'lemon_cms\' AND TABLE_NAME=\'act_app_databasechangeloglock\'\n\nand also with TABLE_SCHEMA = DATABASE() to know current schema name length.\n\nLet me do a combined query.','[{\"id\":\"call_d6a59fad4e5f419aa8d52572\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"确认该表是否在当前库 lemon_cms，还是在同实例其他库\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT DATABASE() AS cur_db,\\\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = \'lemon_cms\' AND TABLE_NAME = \'act_app_databasechangeloglock\') AS in_lemon_cms,\\\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_NAME = \'act_app_databasechangeloglock\') AS in_any_db,\\\\n  (SELECT GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT TABLE_SCHEMA) FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_NAME = \'act_app_databasechangeloglock\') AS schemas_\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_2a213437bbee4c06a05ef567\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"查看 changeloglock 表的字段结构（跨库）\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, ORDINAL_POSITION, COLUMN_NAME, COLUMN_TYPE, IS_NULLABLE, COLUMN_KEY, COLUMN_DEFAULT, COLUMN_COMMENT\\\\nFROM information_schema.COLUMNS\\\\nWHERE TABLE_NAME LIKE \'%databasechangeloglock%\'\\\\nORDER BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, ORDINAL_POSITION\\\"}\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,4376,889,1467891621250176,'2026-09-06 00:59:49'),
