(1467983531893888,1467983199560832,21,'assistant',NULL,'Data is masked. I can see structure hints: 24 rows across schemas (8 columns × 3 schemas?). Actually 24 rows = 3 tables × 8 columns. Each table has 8 columns: ID, LOCKED, LOCK_GRANTER... Liquibase standard DATABASECHANGELOGLOCK has 4 columns (ID, LOCKED, LOCKGRANTED, LOCKEDBY). 8 columns per table? Hmm, 24 rows / 3 tables = 8 columns. Maybe there are 6 tables × 4 columns = 24 rows. Yes! More likely 6 tables with 4 columns each (DATABASECHANGELOGLOCK standard 4 columns) across schemas.\n\nColumn name lengths: 2 chars (ID), 6 chars (LOCKED), 11 chars (LOCKGRANTED is 11!). And LOCKEDBY is 8 chars — not shown in the first 3 rows but there are only 3 distinct rows shown... Actually rows shown are only 3 (masked dedup?). rowCount 24 but only 3 rows displayed? The note says rows desensitized; maybe it deduplicates display. Hmm, displayed 3 rows only. Anyway.\n\nTypes: ID int (7 chars: \"int(11)\" or \"int\" — 7 chars = \"int(11)\"), LOCKED: 6 chars = \"tinyint\"? that\'s 7. \"bit(1)\" is 6 chars. Hmm. LOCKGRANTED: 8 chars = \"datetime\" (8 chars). Yes.\n\nSo this is a Liquibase DATABASECHANGELOGLOCK table. The table `act_app_databasechangeloglock` — likely belongs to a different schema (not lemon_cms). The schemas_ value is 4 chars — masked string of length 4? Actually \"<str:4chars>\" means the value is a 4-char string... but cur_db is \"<str:9chars>\" = \"lemon_cms\" (9 chars). So schemas_ is a 4-char schema name, e.g. \"test\"? And in_lemon_cms is an int (value masked). TABLE_SCHEMA \"<str:4chars>\" for the changelog tables — so those tables live in a 4-char database, not lemon_cms.\n\nWait but the first query returned 3 rows from lemon_cms? TABLE_SCHEMA 4 chars in all 3 rows. Hmm, the query filtered TABLE_NAME LIKE \'%changelog%\' OR \'act_%\' — masked to 3 rows but rowCount 50. So there are 50 matching tables: likely act_* Flowable/Activiti tables plus 3 changelog tables in another schema (4-char schema).\n\nSo `act_app_databasechangeloglock` — 29 chars: let me count: \"act_app_databasechangeloglock\" = 3+1+3+1+18 = 26? a-c-t(3) + _(1)=4 + app(3)=7 + _(1)=8 + databasechangeloglock(21)=29. Yes! 29 chars. So TABLE_NAME \"<str:29chars>\" matches exactly act_app_databasechangeloglock. And it exists in a 4-char schema. The 14-char one: \"DATABASECHANGELOG\" = 17. Hmm \"<str:14chars>\" — maybe \"ACT_APP_DATABASE...\"? Let\'s think: 25 chars and 14 chars. \"act_app_databasechangelog\" = 8 + 19 = 27? databasechangelog = 17 chars → 8+17 = 25. Yes! So the 25-char is act_app_databasechangelog, and 29-char is act_app_databasechangeloglock. The 14-char: \"ACT_APP_DATABASE\"? no. 14 chars... \"databasechangelog\" = 17. Hmm \"lm_...\". Maybe \"ACT_APP_DEPLOY\"? Or \"act_app_database...\"? Let\'s consider: could be \"ACT_APP_DATABASE\"? no that\'s 16. 14 chars: \"act_app_deploy\"? = 14! Yes, \"act_app_deploy\" is 14 chars (act_app_ = 8, deploy = 6 → 14). Plausible for Flowable APP database. Anyway.\n\nSo the table exists in a schema whose name is 4 chars, and in_lemon_cms count is masked int (can\'t read). But schemas_ is 4 chars — meaning the table exists only in a 4-char schema, not lemon_cms (9 chars). So the connected db (lemon_cms) doesn\'t contain it — that\'s why get_table_ddl says table doesn\'t exist.\n\nHmm, but wait: the tool list_tables only lists tables in the connected database. So we can\'t document a table that\'s in another schema... But maybe the masking: schemas_ could be \"lemon_cms,test\" which would be longer than 9 chars. It\'s 4 chars, so a single 4-char schema. So the table is NOT in lemon_cms.\n\nLet me verify by querying with explicit schema filter to get the schema name length and whether lemon_cms has act_ tables. Actually I already know: cur_db = lemon_cms (9 chars), schemas_ = 4 chars. So act_app_databasechangeloglock lives in another database (4-char name), e.g. \"flow\" or \"test\" or \"ruoy\".\n\nI should tell the user: the table isn\'t in the currently connected database lemon_cms, so I can\'t fetch its real structure. But I can still document it based on Liquibase standard structure? Risky — spec says only use real tables/fields. In document mode, save_schema_doc_note requires a table. I could still write the note but must flag it.\n\nLet me do a bit more verification: check whether the 4-char schema\'s table columns match Liquibase standard (ID int PK, LOCKED, LOCKGRANTED, LOCKEDBY). Let me query information_schema with a GROUP_CONCAT of column names to see lengths... but masked. Masking hides real values. Hmm, I can infer lengths via CHAR_LENGTH in aggregate? The masking is based on value type/length. I could compute e.g. SELECT COUNT(*) for specific column names to test hypotheses without revealing data.\n\nLet\'s test: does the table have columns named exactly ID, LOCKED, LOCKGRANTED, LOCKEDBY? Query with WHERE COLUMN_NAME IN (...) and count. If count = 4 → confirms. That\'s a legit approach.\n\nAlso test primary key: COLUMN_KEY=\'PRI\' on ID.\n\nLet me run:\nSELECT TABLE_NAME, COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_NAME=\'act_app_databasechangeloglock\' AND COLUMN_NAME IN (\'ID\',\'LOCKED\',\'LOCKGRANTED\',\'LOCKEDBY\') GROUP BY TABLE_NAME\n\nAnd total column count:\nSELECT TABLE_NAME, COUNT(*) total FROM information_schema.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_NAME LIKE \'%databasechangeloglock%\' GROUP BY TABLE_NAME\n\nLet\'s do both in one query.\n\nAlso check LOCKED type: tinyint(1)/bit(1)/smallint.\n\nAlso, is there a possibility the connected DB is actually the 4-char one and \"lemon_cms\" is masked as 9 chars... cur_db \"<str:9chars>\" = lemon_cms per connection info. Yes.\n\nLet me run the verification query.','[{\"id\":\"call_17ee967e5e394aa2aa1d502f\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"验证该表字段是否符合 Liquibase 标准四列结构，并确认所在库\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME,\\\\n       COUNT(*) AS total_cols,\\\\n       SUM(COLUMN_NAME IN (\'ID\',\'LOCKED\',\'LOCKGRANTED\',\'LOCKEDBY\')) AS std_cols,\\\\n       SUM(COLUMN_KEY=\'PRI\') AS pk_cols,\\\\n       SUM(COLUMN_NAME=\'ID\' AND COLUMN_TYPE LIKE \'int%\') AS id_is_int,\\\\n       SUM(COLUMN_NAME=\'LOCKED\' AND (COLUMN_TYPE LIKE \'bit%\' OR COLUMN_TYPE LIKE \'tinyint%\' OR COLUMN_TYPE LIKE \'smallint%\')) AS locked_type_ok,\\\\n       SUM(COLUMN_NAME=\'LOCKGRANTED\' AND COLUMN_TYPE LIKE \'datetime%\') AS granted_is_datetime\\\\nFROM information_schema.COLUMNS\\\\nWHERE TABLE_NAME IN (\'act_app_databasechangeloglock\',\'act_app_databasechangelog\')\\\\nGROUP BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_d3cc0a2d54a24e2c92383e86\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"确认 act_app_databasechangeloglock 所在库名长度及是否含 lemon_cms\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, CHAR_LENGTH(TABLE_SCHEMA) AS schema_len,\\\\n       (TABLE_SCHEMA = \'lemon_cms\') AS is_current_db,\\\\n       COUNT(*) AS col_cnt\\\\nFROM information_schema.COLUMNS\\\\nWHERE TABLE_NAME = \'act_app_databasechangeloglock\'\\\\nGROUP BY TABLE_SCHEMA\\\"}\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,5092,1911,1467891621250176,'2026-09-06 01:00:08'),
