(1468573761291392,1468573515834496,15,'assistant',NULL,'Data is masked so I can\'t see enum values. DEL_FLAG returned 5 rows across 4 tables — likely values 0/1/2 for some. Standard RuoYi convention: DEL_FLAG 0 = 正常, 2 = 删除 (or 1=删除). I\'ll use `IFNULL(x.DEL_FLAG,0) = 0`? Hmm, safer: `<> 2`? Actually in RuoYi CMS, del_flag 0=存在, 2=删除. But this table comment just says \"删除标识\".\n\nLet me check the count per value without masking — can\'t. I could run a query that returns a boolean-ish aggregate to determine which values exist, e.g. SELECT SUM(DEL_FLAG=0), SUM(DEL_FLAG=1), SUM(DEL_FLAG=2) — but results masked as ints. Masked to \"<int>\", so I can\'t read values. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: use a query whose *row count* or error reveals info? Too hacky. I\'ll go with a safe convention: exclude deleted using `IFNULL(DEL_FLAG, 0) NOT IN (1, 2)`? That could exclude everything if values are odd. Better: use `IFNULL(t.DEL_FLAG,0) = 0` and note in warnings that if the library uses 2 for deletion (RuoYi convention) adjust. Actually `= 0` covers RuoYi\'s 0=正常. And note that if del_flag has other \"normal\" values, adjust.\n\nHmm, but I could determine which values exist via a trick: run a query with HAVING/WHERE and check rowCount. E.g. `SELECT ID FROM lm_cms_channel WHERE DEL_FLAG = 0 LIMIT 1` → rowCount 1 or 0. That reveals existence without exposing data. Let\'s do a few checks: for channel, content, model, site: whether DEL_FLAG=0 rows exist, =1, =2. I can do this with a single query per value using UNION ALL and counting... rowCount is what I see, but rows masked. Actually rowCount is visible! So:\n\nSELECT 1 FROM lm_cms_channel WHERE DEL_FLAG=0 LIMIT 1 → rowCount tells existence.\n\nBetter single query: \nSELECT \'ch0\' k FROM lm_cms_channel WHERE DEL_FLAG=0 LIMIT 1\nUNION ALL SELECT \'ch1\' FROM lm_cms_channel WHERE DEL_FLAG=1 LIMIT 1\n...\nrowCount = number of existing combos, but I won\'t know which ones (rows masked as strings, e.g. \"<str:3chars>\"). Hmm, the masked values lose the key. But maybe masking keeps short strings? It showed \"<str:7chars>\" so no.\n\nAlternative: run separate queries and read rowCount. That\'s ~12 queries. Maybe just do the key ones: check whether DEL_FLAG=0 exists in each table (4 queries) and whether 2 exists (4). Let\'s do a compact approach: run 4 queries in parallel, each returning rowCount via a specific filter.\n\nActually simpler: run one query per table with conditional LIMIT trick? No.\n\nLet me do: for each table, `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t WHERE DEL_FLAG <> 0` — masked int. Row count is 1 always. Not helpful.\n\nUse: `SELECT ID FROM lm_cms_channel WHERE IFNULL(DEL_FLAG,0) <> 0 LIMIT 1` → if rowCount = 0, all rows are 0/normal → filter harmless. If rowCount=1, there exist non-zero values.\n\nThat\'s a good test: 4 queries in parallel. Then also test `WHERE DEL_FLAG = 2 LIMIT 1` to distinguish 1 vs 2 as deletion marker.\n\nLet\'s do 8 parallel calls (4 tables × 2). Actually I can combine per table:\nQuery A: SELECT ID FROM ch WHERE IFNULL(DEL_FLAG,0)<>0 LIMIT 1\nQuery B: SELECT ID FROM ch WHERE DEL_FLAG=2 LIMIT 1\n\nLet me run them.','[{\"id\":\"call_112723aef8ec40d1979b32db\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"判断 lm_cms_channel 是否存在 DEL_FLAG 非 0 的数据\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT ID FROM lemon_cms.lm_cms_channel WHERE IFNULL(DEL_FLAG,0) <> 0 LIMIT 1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_36758d76e6704c7b9b1ba92a\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"判断 lm_cms_content 是否存在 DEL_FLAG 非 0 的数据\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT ID FROM lemon_cms.lm_cms_content WHERE IFNULL(DEL_FLAG,0) <> 0 LIMIT 1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_ee8a24940dea4aaf8bd04bc4\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"判断 lm_cms_model 是否存在 DEL_FLAG 非 0 的数据\\\", \\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT ID FROM lemon_cms.lm_cms_model WHERE IFNULL(DEL_FLAG,0) <> 0 LIMIT 1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_9f82f6fdc0254338a604e2d1\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"判断 lm_cms_site 是否存在 del_flag 非 0 的数