(1470530827797632,1470528714015872,19,'assistant',NULL,'Both quoted-lower and uppercase forms work now — so the alias exists (created via my previous proposal, presumably user ran it, and the object name resolution works both ways... interesting: quoted \"new_function\" works AND NEW_FUNCTION works. That suggests the alias is stored in a case-insensitive manner? In H2, if created with quoted lowercase, calling unquoted NEW_FUNCTION would fail unless DATABASE_TO_LOWER or case-insensitive identifiers setting. Hmm, actually H2 2.x: unquoted identifiers converted to uppercase; quoted kept as-is. If alias created as \"new_function\" (lowercase), then NEW_FUNCTION should not resolve. But it did resolve. Maybe the alias was created as NEW_FUNCTION (uppercase) by the user running an unquoted version, and quoted \"new_function\" resolved because... in H2 2.x, quoted identifiers are case-sensitive, so \"new_function\" shouldn\'t resolve to NEW_FUNCTION. Unless the setting `DATABASE_TO_LOWER`/`CASE_INSENSITIVE_IDENTIFIERS` is on, in which case both resolve.\n\nSo the current state: the function exists and works both ways. So the user\'s reported error \"无法解析函数 new_function\" likely came from a context where the alias didn\'t exist yet — e.g., the DDL was blocked (no 改结构 permission) or executed on a different connection/schema, or they ran it in a session where it wasn\'t created (CREATE ALIAS is session-scoped? No, it\'s database-level for persistent DBs; but for in-memory DBs it\'s per-database). Or maybe they tried running the SELECT before running the CREATE.\n\nHmm, but wait: maybe the error is from a *different* scenario — maybe the user\'s editor still has CREATE ALIAS ... FOR \"java.lang.Math.max\" and they got a different error. I don\'t have the new editor content/selection context this turn (client context only appeared in the first turn... actually the client context block was in the system prompt from turn 1; this turn no updated context given). The user\'s message says \"请根据报错修复 SQL\" with the error being 无法解析函数 new_function (Function new_function not found), presumably.\n\nGiven verification: the function currently resolves fine in this connection. So the most likely cause is that the CREATE ALIAS never actually got executed (blocked by 改结构 permission, or user ran only the SELECT), or it was created in a different database/schema (e.g., in-memory DB restarted, or a different connection).\n\nI should propose a robust final SQL: create the alias without quotes (so name folds to uppercase and works regardless of DATABASE_TO_LOWER settings), with IF NOT EXISTS, and provide the matching call form. Also mention GREATEST fallback.\n\nLet me also verify: does CREATE OR REPLACE ALIAS work? And verify calling with a schema-qualified name. Also verify that unquoted alias + unquoted call works — but I can\'t run DDL. I can verify SELECT NEW_FUNCTION(3,7) works (already does).\n\nLet me check whether the existing alias is schema-qualified: try PUBLIC.NEW_FUNCTION(3,7)? Actually H2 functions in schema. Let me test SELECT \"PUBLIC\".\"NEW_FUNCTION\"(3,7) to see. Not essential.\n\nAlso test GREATEST with mixed NULL to note behavior? Not needed.\n\nOne more useful check: does the alias survive? Let me check INFORMATION_SCHEMA tables available: SHOW SCHEMAS? Let\'s just check which information_schema tables exist for routines: `SELECT * FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.ROUTINES` failed → H2 1.4.200 uses INFORMATION_SCHEMA.FUNCTION_ALIASES or ROUTINES? In 1.4.200, there\'s INFORMATION_SCHEMA.FUNCTION_ALIASES. Let me query that to see actual stored name/case.\n\nAlso SELECT H2VERSION() returned a 7-char string — e.g. \"2.1.214\" is 7 chars, \"1.4.200\" is 7 chars too. Error tags were [90073-200] and [42102-200] → build 200 → H2 1.4.200. In 1.4.200, INFORMATION_SCHEMA.FUNCTION_ALIASES exists.\n\nLet me query it.','[{\"id\":\"call_f77558e3f7a24eeda0981992\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT ALIAS_CATALOG, ALIAS_SCHEMA, ALIAS_N