(1470530948924544,1470528714015872,21,'assistant',NULL,'So alias exists, alias_name is 12 chars → \"new_function\" is 12 chars. So it was created with quoted lowercase name and stored as lowercase. Both quoted and unquoted calls work (H2 1.4.200 is case-insensitive for function lookup? Actually unquoted NEW_FUNCTION worked too — H2 1.4.200 resolves aliases case-insensitively).\n\nSo the user\'s error \"Function not found: new_function\" — where could it come from? Possibly they ran in a different context: e.g., the client\'s \"查询按钮\" ran against a different database (in-memory new connection), or they used a fully-qualified name \"PUBLIC\".\"new_function\", or they ran in a session where alias doesn\'t exist (H2 in-memory DB re-created per connection). Or maybe they ran the SELECT in a different connection/schema.\n\nHmm, but also possible: the error came from a different SQL statement — perhaps they wrote something like SELECT new_function(...) but with a schema qualifier, or they used it in a WHERE/ORDER context. Or maybe the error is from H2 2.x semantics: in H2 2.x, quoted identifiers are case-sensitive, so \"new_function\" would be stored lowercase and unquoted new_function → NEW_FUNCTION not found. But here both worked, so this instance is H2 1.4.200 (error suffix -200 matches 1.4.200).\n\nWait — the error text says \"Function not found: new_function\" (lowercase). In H2 1.4.200, the message prints the name as resolved... Actually in H2, when a function isn\'t found the message shows the uppercased name typically: \"Function not found NEW_FUNCTION\". Showing lowercase \"new_function\" suggests the user\'s H2 session has a different case-sensitivity setting, e.g., DATABASE_TO_LOWER=TRUE or CASE_INSENSITIVE_IDENTIFIERS... Or the user is executing against a *different* connection/database where the alias was never created (aliases are per-database; if the connection is in-memory mem:test DB, each new connection may recreate a fresh DB).\n\nGiven ambiguity, the robust fix: don\'t depend on the alias at all — use the built-in GREATEST (verified working). Also provide a re-creatable DDL with unquoted name and DROP IF EXISTS first, plus a note that aliases are stored per database and are lost if the connection points to a fresh in-memory DB or a different catalog/schema.\n\nAlso I should mention: verify the alias exists via INFORMATION_SCHEMA.FUNCTION_ALIASES (that\'s the correct table in this H2 version; ALIASES/ROUTINES don\'t exist).\n\nLet me also verify GREATEST works with two args of different types, and that a schema-qualified call works: SELECT PUBLIC.NEW_FUNCTION(3,7)? Let\'s test a couple of variants to give accurate guidance.\n\nLet me test: SELECT \"PUBLIC\".\"new_function\"(3,7) — hmm, function with schema qualifier. And test DROP + CREATE unquoted. But DDL can\'t be run via run_sql. So just test the qualified call.','[{\"id\":\"call_54b264c20303482d91c97bf0\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT PUBLIC.NEW_FUNCTION(3, 7) AS qualified_call\\\", \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"验证带模式限定名调用是否可用\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"call_44d10645f8554db89b2878f4\",\"name\":\"run_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"sql\\\": \\\"SELECT GREATEST(3, 7) AS builtin_greatest, GREATEST(2.5, 8.1) AS decimal_greatest\\\", \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"确认内置替代方案稳定可用（整数与小数）\\\"}\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,6109,810,1467891621250176,'2026-09-09 15:22:52'),
