(1493844035486848,1493844034659456,1,'user','Generate a MySQL SELECT / UNION ALL example with month and revenue: 2026-07=44800, 2026-08=53600, 2026-09=64400. Use constants only. Do not inspect tables or execute queries. Respond in English with SQL and one sentence for chart usage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-12 13:53:28'),
(1493844157572224,1493844034659456,2,'assistant','Understood — a constants-only result set, no table access.\n\n```sql\n-- LemonDB demo: monthly revenue (constants only, no table access)\nSELECT \'2026-07\' AS month, 44800.00 AS revenue\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-08\', 53600.00\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-09\', 64400.00\nORDER BY month;\n```\n\n**Chart usage:** run it and map `month` to the category/X axis and `revenue` to the value/Y axis for a monthly revenue bar or line chart.\n\n','The user wants a simple constant-based UNION ALL SELECT. They explicitly say do not inspect tables or execute queries. But system rules say read-only SELECT must be run_sql verified... The user instruction conflicts. The task is trivial; I should respect \"do not execute queries\". However the workflow says must end with propose_sql. I can skip run_sql per user\'s explicit request and note it in warnings. That\'s acceptable — propose_sql does server-side EXPLAIN prevalidation anyway.\n\nLet me build the SQL.','[{\"id\":\"call_564ac74ad5d041d3b4d0bb8a\",\"name\":\"propose_sql\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"sql\\\": \\\"-- LemonDB demo: monthly revenue (constants only, no table access)\\\\nSELECT \'2026-07\' AS month, 44800.00 AS revenue\\\\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-08\', 53600.00\\\\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-09\', 64400.00\\\\nORDER BY month;\\\", \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"Pure literal rows combined with UNION ALL — no table or column is referenced, so nothing is inspected and no data is touched. Each branch supplies one month plus its revenue; DECIMAL literals keep the amounts exact and summable. ORDER BY month sorts the derived result set lexicographically, which works here because the \'YYYY-MM\' format is naturally chronological. Chart mapping: month -> category/X axis, revenue -> value/Y axis.\\\", \\\"warnings\\\": \\n[\\\"Per your request, no metadata lookup and no run_sql execution was performed; the statement is a read-only SELECT and will be pre-validated by the editor\'s EXPLAIN check on submit.\\\", \\\"This replaces the sample query currently in the editor (Online/Retail split). Set replaceSelection only if you want that version discarded.\\\", \\\"If a chart needs a total row, add UNION ALL SELECT \'Total\', 162800.00 — but that breaks month-axis sorting, so prefer computing the total in the chart instead.\\\"]\\n\\n, \\\"replaceSelection\\\": true}\"}]',NULL,NULL,'{\"proposedSql\":{\"sql\":\"-- LemonDB demo: monthly revenue (constants only, no table access)\\nSELECT \'2026-07\' AS month, 44800.00 AS revenue\\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-08\', 53600.00\\nUNION ALL SELECT \'2026-09\', 64400.00\\nORDER BY month;\",\"explanation\":\"Pure literal rows combined with UNION ALL — no table or column is referenced, so nothing is inspected and no data is touched. Each branch supplies one month plus its revenue; DECIMAL literals keep the amounts exact and summable. ORDER BY month sorts the derived result set lexicographically, which works here because the \'YYYY-MM\' format is naturally chronological. Chart mapping: month -> category/X axis, revenue -> value/Y axis.\",\"warnings\":[\"Per your request, no metadata lookup and no run_sql execution was performed; the statement is a read-only SELECT and will be pre-validated by the editor\'s EXPLAIN check on submit.\",\"This replaces the sample query currently in the editor (Online/Retail split). Set replaceSelection only if you want that version discarded.\",\"If a chart needs a total row, add UNION ALL SELECT \'Total\', 162800.00 — but that breaks month-axis sorting, so prefer computing the total in the chart instead.\"],\"writeOperation\":false,\"replaceSelection\":true,\"validation\":{\"status\":\"passed\",\"method\":\"explain\"}}}',5334,601,1467891621250176,'2026-10-12 13:53:43'),
